# Toolbox — everything the agents get on the box, in one editable list.
#
#   <channel>  <package>                    [binary]
#
# channel  where it comes from
#   apt    Debian package, installed into the image at build time
#   npm    global npm package, installed into the image at build time
#   brew   Homebrew formula, installed at runtime into the persistent volume
#          (requires AGENTBOARD_ENABLE_BREW=1 — see install-brew.sh)
#
# binary   optional; when given, the installer verifies it landed on PATH and
#          warns if it did not. For agents this MUST match the name the board
#          probes for, or the agent shows as unavailable.
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Add to this file and redeploy — nothing
# else needs to change.

# --- Agent CLIs -------------------------------------------------------------
# The board probes PATH for exactly these binaries (agent-sdk-core
# providers/detection.js calls checkCLI on each name).
npm   @anthropic-ai/claude-code   claude
npm   @github/copilot             copilot
npm   @openai/codex               codex
npm   opencode-ai                 opencode
npm   openclaw                    openclaw

# Hermes is deliberately NOT listed. The board probes for a `hermes` binary,
# but the npm package of that name is segmentio's "Messenger of the gods" and
# `hermes-cli` searches Brazilian travel agencies — installing either would put
# a bogus `hermes` on PATH and make the board report Hermes as available when
# it is not. Add the real install line here once you know it; the README says
# the check is `hermes acp --check`.
# npm  <real-hermes-package>       hermes

# --- Source control and shell tools the agents actually reach for ------------
apt   ripgrep                     rg
apt   fd-find
apt   jq                          jq
apt   less                        less
apt   tree                        tree
apt   unzip                       unzip
apt   openssh-client              ssh
apt   ca-certificates

# --- Optional extras, installed via Homebrew at runtime ---------------------
# These persist on the data volume across deploys and instance replacement.
# Uncomment what you want; agents can also `brew install` more themselves.
# brew  gh
# brew  bat
# brew  yq
